This file records the third-party projects this codebase references, the license each
one carries, and the obligations that attach. It exists because the Apache-2.0
libraries below require attribution and a statement of changes, and because one of our
data sources imposes a condition on how its data may be displayed.


THIRD-PARTY LIBRARIES
=====================

Crawl4AI — Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/unclecode/crawl4ai
  LLM-ready web crawler. Considered for browser-rendering of JS-heavy listing pages.
  Status: referenced only, NOT a dependency of v1. Every source we ingest returns JSON
  over plain HTTP, so there is no JavaScript page to render. Adopting it now would buy
  a browser download in CI and nothing else. The seam is reserved for a future HTML
  detail-page enrichment path that would raise pay coverage, and is adopted only if a
  measured sample of target pages justifies it.
  Apache-2.0 obligations: none are triggered by v1, because the code is not
  redistributed here. If it is added later, its notice and license ship with the
  dependency and any local modification must be described in this file.

Better Auth — MIT License
  https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth
  Framework-agnostic authentication library for TypeScript. Used for Google sign-in, self-hosted, with its tables
  in the same Postgres database as the rest of the app. Sign-in is limited to an invite list.
  Status: adopted.
  MIT obligations: the copyright notice and license text ship with the dependency and
  are reproduced by its own distribution. This project uses it unmodified.


DATA SOURCE ATTRIBUTION
=======================

Himalayas — public search API, https://himalayas.app/jobs/api/search
  Used for one saved query (India, entry level, full-time, remote). Its terms ask that the source is shown and that
  its jobs are not resubmitted to other job platforms. This project shows "via Himalayas" on every job from it,
  sends the person to the Himalayas page to apply, and never reposts its jobs. Requests are paced at one per two
  seconds and stop on a 429 answer.

Company job boards — Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, SmartRecruiters, Workable, Recruitee
  Read through each platform's public, key-less posting endpoints, one polite request at a time. Every job links to
  the employer's own apply page.

Not used: Remote OK, Jobicy and Remotive. Earlier versions of this project read Remote OK and Jobicy; their code and
attribution obligations were removed with them. Remotive's terms forbid republishing its jobs, so it is not collected.

No platform requiring login to a personal account is scraped by this project. See docs/sources-terms.md.
